// TheScanner deployment config — Cloudflare Workers with Static Assets
// (ADR-0029, corrected framing per Session 15's task prompt: Cloudflare
// unified "Pages" into this path — there is no separate web-UI "build
// output directory" setting anymore, this file is what tells Cloudflare
// what to serve).
//
// assets.directory points at pwa/, not the repo root — see run.py and
// ARCHITECTURE.md §9a for why latest_scan.json/usage_summary.json were
// moved to live inside pwa/ this session: only files inside this
// directory are ever reachable on the deployed site, and Cloudflare's
// Git-integration flow redeploys (re-snapshotting this directory) on
// every push, including the scan workflow's own commit-back push.
//
// Session 33 adds `main`: a real Worker script (worker/index.js) now
// coexists with the static assets above, for the push-subscribe/
// trigger-scan/notify API routes (ARCHITECTURE.md §11). Confirmed via
// Cloudflare's current docs, not assumed: `assets.run_worker_first`
// defaults to `false`, meaning a request matching a real file under
// `pwa/` is still served as a static asset exactly as before this
// session, and the Worker's fetch handler only ever runs for a request
// that matched no asset at all — true for all three new API paths, so
// no extra `run_worker_first` config is needed here.
//
// kv_namespaces is NOT added yet — the real "thescanner-subscriptions"
// namespace doesn't exist in Cloudflare yet as of Session 33 (confirmed
// with Elad directly, not assumed). Once it's created, add:
//   "kv_namespaces": [ { "binding": "SUBSCRIPTIONS", "id": "<real 32-char hex namespace ID from the Cloudflare dashboard>" } ]
// worker/index.js already expects `env.SUBSCRIPTIONS` under exactly that
// binding name.
{
  "name": "thescanner",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-11",
  "main": "./worker/index.js",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./pwa"
  }
}
